WEBVTT

00:07.520 --> 00:10.090
We've caught the ire of a troublesome foe.

00:10.090 --> 00:12.950
There is only on type of
dragon that breathes fire.

00:13.460 --> 00:16.200
The masters of the Kurogane Mountains...

00:16.200 --> 00:19.080
The flame dragons—
a strain of true dragons—

00:20.620 --> 00:22.290
the Guren Nairi!

00:23.080 --> 00:26.360
A true dragon? Then it's as
dangerous as a Morisuberi?

00:26.360 --> 00:27.720
Yes. The difference being...

00:35.470 --> 00:38.340
This one is neither wounded,
like the Morisuberi was,

00:38.340 --> 00:40.730
nor do we have a group
of over ten warriors!

00:40.980 --> 00:45.880
If we face it head-on you and I may
survive, but Malcius and Cersei will die!

00:45.880 --> 00:46.610
Die?!

00:46.920 --> 00:50.870
Is there anything we can do? Does the
Echo Dragon breathe fire as well?

00:50.870 --> 00:54.020
This spirit is the embodiment
of our yearning for flight.

00:54.020 --> 00:55.620
And flight is the only thing it offers.

00:55.620 --> 00:58.070
It seems we have no choice but
to land and face it in battle.

00:58.070 --> 01:00.270
Two against a fire dragon is madness!

01:00.270 --> 01:04.250
You don't even have a helmet!
The best choice is to flee.

01:04.250 --> 01:07.880
A fire dragon shouldn't take any interest
in a mock dragon in the first place.

01:07.880 --> 01:09.020
Why is this happening?

01:17.400 --> 01:18.140
What was that?!

01:22.900 --> 01:24.580
The Quefto's anti-dragon guns.

01:24.580 --> 01:26.430
They don't seem to be working!

01:26.430 --> 01:28.010
A distraction is all we need!

01:28.010 --> 01:29.150
We're landing!

01:50.920 --> 01:58.560
The Warrior Princess and the Barbaric King

03:26.700 --> 03:28.690
Dying! I'm dying!

03:29.190 --> 03:30.900
Lord Thundering Voice, are you all right?

03:30.900 --> 03:32.710
I appreciate the assist!

03:32.940 --> 03:35.640
But given who our foe is,
I don't like our odds.

03:35.640 --> 03:37.590
The sooner we lose it, the better.

03:37.590 --> 03:41.080
Understood. Everyone,
leave the guns and clear out!

03:41.400 --> 03:43.680
Withdraw into tunnel four!

03:45.790 --> 03:47.600
This way, ladies.

03:47.600 --> 03:48.660
But...

03:53.070 --> 03:54.960
You won't wanna look at it!

03:55.710 --> 04:00.340
Have a taste of Quefto hunter technology!

04:06.600 --> 04:08.100
Sera! Run!

04:18.740 --> 04:21.240
Sera! Hold your breath and get down!

04:56.750 --> 04:59.750
I think we managed to get away.

04:59.750 --> 05:01.700
So it seems.

05:06.040 --> 05:08.350
Are you hurt, Sera?

05:08.960 --> 05:10.330
No, thanks to you.

05:10.570 --> 05:13.830
But what about you?
Considering what happened.

05:14.060 --> 05:17.160
Just a bit singed. Nothing serious.

05:17.530 --> 05:19.090
Lady Serafina!

05:19.360 --> 05:21.420
Are you two all right?

05:25.920 --> 05:27.600
I'm glad you're all unhurt, too.

05:30.140 --> 05:36.300
Have to say, when the watchman came to
sound the alert, I was really shocked.

05:36.300 --> 05:40.740
We would've experienced losses without
the Quefto's support. I'm grateful.

05:40.950 --> 05:43.630
Is it rare to run into those things?

05:43.630 --> 05:47.180
Usually. They tend to keep to
the inside of the crater...

05:47.620 --> 05:50.500
I would've never expected one
this far down the mountain.

05:50.500 --> 05:54.580
I mean, who knows what goes
on in a dragon's head?

05:54.580 --> 05:58.180
For now, let's be grateful
that everybody survived.

05:58.180 --> 05:59.250
You're right.

05:59.530 --> 06:01.470
And here we are.

06:22.500 --> 06:26.100
And this is the dwarves' village?

06:28.110 --> 06:33.040
Welcome to the home of the
Quefto, Furnace Ridge!

06:33.560 --> 06:36.680
To bore so cleanly into
the foot of a mountain...

06:36.680 --> 06:39.550
I can't imagine the technology
and effort that was involved.

06:40.920 --> 06:44.550
Kinda hard to resist being proud,
when you put it that way.

06:44.550 --> 06:48.550
After all, there's nothing we Quefto
enjoy more than digging and research.

06:49.180 --> 06:52.060
I see. That is very dwarf-like.

06:52.590 --> 06:56.630
I should've given my name earlier.
It's Serafina de Lavillant.

06:56.630 --> 06:59.330
The way you blinded the
dragon was brilliant.

06:59.330 --> 07:02.400
Aw, you don't have to be
so formal with your praise,

07:02.400 --> 07:04.840
you're making me feel itchy.

07:04.840 --> 07:06.800
Don't worry about manners with me.

07:08.240 --> 07:12.190
My name is Kimaki. It's nice to meet you.

07:12.190 --> 07:14.710
Right. It's a pleasure, Sir Kimaki.

07:15.180 --> 07:17.070
Aw, don't call me sir!

07:18.870 --> 07:24.640
All right, I figure swapping names might
be a sign. I'll show our guests around!

07:24.640 --> 07:25.860
No fair, Kimaki.

07:25.860 --> 07:26.790
So jealous.

07:26.790 --> 07:28.340
First come, first served!

07:28.680 --> 07:30.790
You're just gonna get lost, anyway!

07:30.790 --> 07:34.670
Yeah, if you show them around,
we might never see them again!

07:32.200 --> 07:35.560
It's a shame after
exchanging names, but...

07:35.560 --> 07:37.850
it's really hard to tell them apart.

07:44.270 --> 07:49.360
It's so hot...
and what's this strange smell?

07:49.620 --> 07:51.380
It's sulfur.

07:51.380 --> 07:54.900
Sulfur? Like what's used in gunpowder?

07:54.900 --> 07:57.120
I believe I read about it in
a military textbook once.

07:57.410 --> 08:00.000
m 10 0 l 185 0 l 195 10 l 195 65 l 185 75 l 185 75 l 10 75 l 0 65 l 0 10

07:57.410 --> 08:00.000
It's actually hydrogen sulfide
that has a strong odor;
solid sulfur is odorless.

08:02.060 --> 08:03.960
Here we are, folks!

08:04.660 --> 08:08.470
Say hello to the source of the
Quefto settlement's hot springs!

08:14.270 --> 08:17.300
I-It really is natural hot water.

08:17.300 --> 08:20.520
I-It's so fantastical!

08:20.520 --> 08:23.300
Is this your first time at a hot spring?

08:23.300 --> 08:25.030
I'd been told about them, but...

08:26.440 --> 08:28.990
Well, as you can see, it's boiling hot...

08:28.990 --> 08:31.780
Over there, we cool it
down to be just right.

08:34.650 --> 08:36.710
Sera. I'll see you later.

08:36.710 --> 08:39.540
Right, of course we'd separate here...

08:40.400 --> 08:42.810
Were you hoping to bathe with Master Veor?

08:42.810 --> 08:45.010
I-I said no such thing!

08:46.090 --> 08:47.960
It's Quefto culture.

08:47.960 --> 08:49.180
For whatever reason,

08:49.180 --> 08:52.870
they have separate changing areas
and entrances for men and women.

08:52.870 --> 08:57.060
I find your lack of pretension
to be much stranger.

08:59.440 --> 09:00.590
Right this way.

09:01.840 --> 09:05.070
Maybe it's because it's for dwarves,
but the ceiling is awfully low.

09:06.160 --> 09:08.570
Everything is made of metal.

09:09.200 --> 09:11.500
Wood long enough for 
construction is pretty valuable

09:11.500 --> 09:13.820
because of how much trouble
it is to bring it in.

09:14.500 --> 09:17.860
But there's a ton of stone and metal,

09:17.860 --> 09:21.330
so we naturally ended up living
in these kinds of buildings.

09:21.590 --> 09:24.290
I suppose that's simply
the regional flavor.

09:24.290 --> 09:27.540
I can help you take your armor off, Sera.

09:27.540 --> 09:28.940
Me too!

09:28.940 --> 09:30.340
Yes, please.

09:33.560 --> 09:36.140
But a hot spring, eh?

09:37.070 --> 09:41.710
A natural bath... I can only
wonder what it must feel like.

09:53.750 --> 09:58.270
What happened to men and women bathing
separately?! And you're being so brazen!

09:58.910 --> 10:02.320
Well, Kimaki, even if you are a child...

10:02.320 --> 10:04.350
watching someone get undressed is a bit...

10:06.200 --> 10:07.840
H-Hang on a sec!

10:07.840 --> 10:11.010
I wonder if my gear
muffled my voice some...

10:18.030 --> 10:20.520
That's better, isn't it?

10:21.460 --> 10:24.810
Wh-What?! You still don't believe me?

10:24.810 --> 10:26.860
How about this, then?!

10:29.780 --> 10:32.530
She's a girl?!

10:32.750 --> 10:36.530
"Girl?" I actually turned
55 this year, y'know.

10:36.530 --> 10:39.280
Fifty...?! You're older?!

10:39.670 --> 10:42.890
Well, in Cornem years,
it'd be more like 20.

10:42.890 --> 10:47.290
Another shocked westerner told me
I looked like a kid before.

10:48.110 --> 10:51.710
We don't all have beards, y'know!
Don't make assumptions!

10:53.540 --> 10:58.430
I-It's more based off of an
old story about your kind...

10:59.590 --> 11:03.510
There's a good chance our scarves are
where the beard stories came from, then.

11:03.510 --> 11:05.090
Considering where we live, it's important

11:05.090 --> 11:07.440
for everyone to have protection
against poison gas and dust.

11:07.740 --> 11:10.190
I suppose stories that get passed
down do have that tendency.

11:12.410 --> 11:15.710
The way you're reacting...
It's been a while.

11:15.710 --> 11:19.780
You knew this was going to happen
and didn't say anything, didn't you?

11:19.780 --> 11:24.200
It reminds me of when
Master Veor first brought you in!

11:24.460 --> 11:28.960
But why were you staring at
Lady Serafina as she was changing?

11:28.960 --> 11:31.090
I was looking at that.

11:31.880 --> 11:32.960
My armor?

11:33.520 --> 11:35.470
Miss Sera...

11:35.470 --> 11:40.380
Not that I need repayment
for the hospitality, but...

11:40.380 --> 11:45.480
Would it be okay if I took apart and
did some upkeep on your armor...?

11:45.480 --> 11:50.570
Uh... if you're going to maintain it,
I'd honestly be willing to pay you.

11:50.570 --> 11:51.980
I couldn't ask for that!

11:52.380 --> 11:53.530
Because...

11:53.980 --> 11:55.870
'Cuz...

11:56.700 --> 12:02.560
It'd be rude of me not to lay
hands on such a sexy work of art!

12:02.560 --> 12:05.750
Sh-She's a woman of particular tastes!

12:06.980 --> 12:10.000
Point being, we're all slaves
to our passions down here.

12:10.260 --> 12:12.090
Unique works of craftsmanship,

12:12.090 --> 12:13.910
the study of technology
and rare materials,

12:13.910 --> 12:15.900

even science in the broad sense...

12:15.900 --> 12:19.010
We crave to learn all we can about
 anything that catches our interest!

12:19.280 --> 12:22.410
And whenever we meet someone who gives
us a chance to indulge our curiosity,

12:22.410 --> 12:23.760
we love to host them!

12:24.390 --> 12:25.720
Kimaki...

12:26.270 --> 12:28.990
Understood. Study it as much as you want.

12:28.990 --> 12:29.900
Yay!

12:30.260 --> 12:31.650
Seriously?!

12:31.870 --> 12:33.540
Look at it shine!

12:32.330 --> 12:33.540
Amazing!

12:33.540 --> 12:34.650
Damn!

12:34.650 --> 12:37.640
Thanks a bunch, Crystal Helmet!

12:37.640 --> 12:39.910
I'll be along to get a feel later!

12:43.260 --> 12:46.370
What happened to the
separation of sexes?

12:53.130 --> 12:54.480
It's huge!

12:54.480 --> 12:57.550
H-How much firewood 
would this luxury cost?

13:00.480 --> 13:03.360
It really is a natural bath.

13:03.360 --> 13:05.810
Does the water seem cloudy to you?

13:05.810 --> 13:09.100
Those are crystals from melted sulfur.

13:09.100 --> 13:11.920
There's sulfur in the water?!

13:11.920 --> 13:13.440
It's a good thing!

13:13.440 --> 13:21.950
Medicinal Usage for Sulfur Springs:

13:13.750 --> 13:17.880
It helps with stamina recovery,
healing cuts, burns, and bad circulation.

13:15.000 --> 13:21.950
- Chronic skin disease

- Chronic gynopathy

13:16.500 --> 13:21.950
- Cuts

- Lifestyle-related diseases

13:17.880 --> 13:20.280
It's supposedly great for the skin, too.

13:20.280 --> 13:21.950
We owe it all to the sulfur!

13:22.190 --> 13:25.950
Th-Then this whole
thing is a medicinal bath?

13:25.950 --> 13:28.270
I suppose it is.

13:28.270 --> 13:30.210
And it's all natural...!

13:30.590 --> 13:35.130
For your information, these waters have
been flowing for at least 2000 years.

13:35.130 --> 13:37.690
That's longer than Illdoren has exited...

13:37.690 --> 13:40.970
Maybe it's best to not think about it.

13:51.320 --> 13:53.730
This is fantastic!

13:53.730 --> 13:57.660
It's certainly different from
washing off in rivers or lakes.

13:57.660 --> 14:01.420
The last time I came here was with the
great chief's wife, and it's still good.

14:01.420 --> 14:02.740
You came with Resia?

14:04.030 --> 14:06.700
Can she use the Echo Dragon too?

14:08.620 --> 14:10.370
Yes, she certainly can.

14:10.600 --> 14:11.930
But how...?

14:11.930 --> 14:13.150
You earn the right to summon it

14:13.150 --> 14:15.880
by defeating a dragon
on your own, apparently.

14:16.250 --> 14:19.280
I'm sure you know how
competitive she can be.

14:19.280 --> 14:23.130
She couldn't resist the chance
to prove herself to a spirit.

14:23.510 --> 14:27.110
A symbol of strength... like the
dragon knights out of a fairy tale!

14:27.110 --> 14:28.390
I want that, too!

14:28.620 --> 14:30.490
No, it's a bad idea.

14:30.490 --> 14:33.210
Even for someone who was able to fight
a dragon with a pair of fire tongs,

14:33.210 --> 14:34.240
it's dangerous!

14:34.240 --> 14:35.300
It's dangerous?!

14:35.830 --> 14:37.890
Wanting to hunt a
dragon single-handedly...

14:37.890 --> 14:40.400
You Cornem sure like to live on the edge.

14:44.190 --> 14:46.080
Look at that.

14:46.080 --> 14:49.030
Feels nice, doesn't it?

14:50.270 --> 14:54.670
I know that we're underground,
but it's still fairly bright.

14:55.290 --> 14:57.650
Like looking at a starry sky.

14:57.650 --> 15:00.170
That shine is coming from the True Silver.

15:01.350 --> 15:03.440
All of that is mythril?!

15:04.090 --> 15:06.180
Just a pinch of it, really.

15:06.790 --> 15:11.820
True Silver glows because it's
affected by the volcano's willpower.

15:11.820 --> 15:13.510
It's gentler than sunlight,

15:13.510 --> 15:16.810
and valuable to us since we
don't do well with bright light.

15:17.060 --> 15:20.260
That boulder over there
is also True Silver.

15:22.570 --> 15:24.820
It hasn't been refined,
so it's a bit cloudy...

15:24.820 --> 15:26.220
But if a Cornem warrior like you,

15:26.220 --> 15:29.470
Miss Sera, channels her willpower
through it, it'll light up!

15:30.260 --> 15:32.330
I see! Okay!

15:33.020 --> 15:34.960
Let's try it right now!

15:35.280 --> 15:37.100
But that's—

15:39.310 --> 15:40.340
Oh, well.

15:48.310 --> 15:50.100
When I touched the stone...

15:50.700 --> 15:54.890
I don't know how to describe 
what it made me feel deep inside.

15:58.880 --> 16:01.360
It wasn't like the willpower that
is channeled through a weapon...

16:02.340 --> 16:06.040
Or the curiosity I felt
just a few moments ago...

16:20.710 --> 16:23.090
Nostalgia so strong as to
bring tears to the eyes...

16:23.820 --> 16:25.140
Longing?

16:28.270 --> 16:31.010
What was that?! Is the heat getting to me?

16:42.070 --> 16:45.020
How can I yearn for scenery
I've never seen before?

16:46.480 --> 16:48.180
S-Sera?

16:59.180 --> 17:01.880
Ve..o...r...?

17:01.880 --> 17:04.790
I-I thought you were somewhere else?!

17:04.790 --> 17:08.550
I told you that the changing
rooms are separate...

17:09.350 --> 17:11.710
Then everyone is funneled
into the same baths?!

17:13.070 --> 17:14.800
Get away from her, barbarian!

17:15.550 --> 17:17.600
The only way those two will get closer

17:17.600 --> 17:20.120
is if "accidents" like
these keep happening.

17:20.120 --> 17:22.440
Wait, they're not together?

17:22.440 --> 17:24.940
I had the wrong idea...

17:24.940 --> 17:26.980
And, uh, I must say...

17:37.390 --> 17:39.450
You are one bold woman!

17:40.480 --> 17:41.830
A dragon?!

17:41.830 --> 17:46.230
Wh-Why is it even bigger?!

17:48.710 --> 17:50.970
Lady Serafina!

17:50.970 --> 17:54.890
I will defend your virtue!

18:03.200 --> 18:05.430
Even if I am engaged to him,

18:05.430 --> 18:09.470
I feel that, as a maiden, I lost
something irreplaceable today...

18:12.650 --> 18:14.480
Where's your armor?

18:15.110 --> 18:17.490
The Quefto took it.

18:20.120 --> 18:22.130
How's Malcius doing?

18:22.910 --> 18:26.080
I think she got overheated,
in more ways than one.

18:27.030 --> 18:29.000
Lady Serafina...

18:35.010 --> 18:38.620
I can't deny that I got
a bit overheated, myself.

18:44.300 --> 18:45.270
Is that from earlier?!

18:47.520 --> 18:52.530
That's "a bit singed"?
He was burned protecting me.

18:53.030 --> 18:56.350
Veor... you really are impressive.

19:02.150 --> 19:03.290
She noticed...

19:04.180 --> 19:07.790
I can never seem to impress
in the way I intend to.

19:10.960 --> 19:14.060
But you're no less impressive for it.

19:21.290 --> 19:24.560
Here you are, Lord Thunder
Voice and his party!

19:24.560 --> 19:27.060
Our village's specialty dishes!

19:27.360 --> 19:29.110
Boiled hot springs crab,

19:29.430 --> 19:31.570
alcohol-steamed mountain snails...

19:32.060 --> 19:34.570
and the local staple,
hillside potato mochi!

19:36.230 --> 19:38.070
Dwarven cuisine!

19:38.070 --> 19:41.440
The hot springs crabs live in the
hot springs, as the name suggests,

19:41.440 --> 19:44.780
which gives them a unique aroma,
but they're delicious!

19:44.780 --> 19:48.690
The mountain snails are a kind of
snail that you can find in these parts.

19:49.310 --> 19:51.350
After a preparatory boiling,
you take out the innards,

19:51.350 --> 19:53.740
and then steam the flesh with alcohol.

19:53.740 --> 19:55.220
Snails...?

19:55.470 --> 20:00.340
The hillside potatoes grow all around
the mountain in huge amounts,

20:00.340 --> 20:04.850
so apart from being a staple food,
we use it to make our alcohol.

20:04.850 --> 20:06.390
Tell me, Sera,

20:06.390 --> 20:10.270
what is the the drink that the Quefto
prefer in your western stories?

20:10.920 --> 20:13.860
Dwarven fire wine?!
You actually have some?!

20:14.800 --> 20:16.240
You bet we do!

20:19.490 --> 20:22.250
What a beautiful copper-gold color...

20:22.750 --> 20:26.750
And I don't think I've ever smelt
such strong spirits before!

20:27.040 --> 20:32.750
The distilling process for pharmacology
was how we learned how to make it.

20:39.610 --> 20:42.640
So deliciously spicy!

20:43.020 --> 20:45.880
Try this. It goes well with the wine.

20:51.560 --> 20:53.820
Good! Fantastic!

20:53.820 --> 20:55.350
Try this, too.

20:55.350 --> 20:56.890
Gladly!

20:57.780 --> 21:03.130
Every single food I've tried is amazing!
Something is strange with this land!

21:04.910 --> 21:05.660
Here.

21:05.660 --> 21:07.180
A sip of fire wine, and then...

21:11.040 --> 21:12.870
It's so good!

21:12.870 --> 21:15.550
I think that incident
had a positive effect.

21:15.550 --> 21:18.280
Naked intimacy leading
to new developments...!

21:20.280 --> 21:22.110
Veor, I want to try the potato mochi next!

21:22.110 --> 21:24.300
Chew slowly, so you don't choke.

21:25.790 --> 21:28.180
Give me another, Veor!

21:28.850 --> 21:31.600
Translation: Lee Francis

Timing: Andy Ellis

Editing: Zachary Carlysle

Quality Control: Salem Alabanza

Translation Check: Sho Stifler

23:03.930 --> 23:08.200
I must say, I may have overeaten a bit.

23:08.200 --> 23:11.270
Four crabs, twelve mountain snails,

23:11.270 --> 23:14.750
and nine pieces of
potato mochi... is a bit?

23:15.440 --> 23:19.210
We were just glad you seemed to like it.

23:20.460 --> 23:23.210
We appreciate the heartfelt feast, Kimaki.

23:23.210 --> 23:26.310
I bathed in the hot springs
and ate my fill.

23:26.310 --> 23:31.720
Now it's time for the objective of
this trip—collecting my helmet!

23:32.160 --> 23:35.450
Off we go to the dwarven workshop!
